### A relation rule: `visits.rules.list/get` admit a technician through the JOB —
### `work_order_id.assigned_to == @user.id` — and the related entity's own list rule applies too.
### Reads only; the rows are 140-Integrity/004's: two tech-north visits on WO-3401 (assigned to
### tech-north) and one spare-north visit on WO-3402 (assigned to nobody).
###
### spare-north being the 3402 visit's `technician_id` yet NOT seeing it is deliberate: the relation, not
### the `technician_id` column, decides visibility. The job is nobody's, so its visit is nobody's.

### tech-north's visits
# @name TechLists
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits?order=starts_at.asc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyTechNorth}}

### spare-north's visits: the same rule, a technician with no job assigned
# @name SpareLists
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits?order=starts_at.asc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keySpareNorth}}

### The dispatcher's: every visit in the tenant (control — the rows exist)
# @name DispatcherLists
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits?order=starts_at.asc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### tech-north reads the 3402 visit by id: one row failing the rule is 404, never 403
# @name TechReadsOthersVisit
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [404]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits/{{VisitOnUnassignedJobId}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyTechNorth}}

### The same id read by the dispatcher (control — the 404 is the rule, not a missing row)
# @name DispatcherReadsThatVisit
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits/{{VisitOnUnassignedJobId}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### WRITES, after every read above. `visits.update` is the read rule plus being the booked technician:
### `technician_id == @user.id && work_order_id.assigned_to == @user.id`. spare-north IS the 3402 visit's
### technician, but the job is nobody's — so they may not write a visit they cannot read
# @name SpareWritesUnassignedVisit
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [404]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits/{{VisitOnUnassignedJobId}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keySpareNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "minutes_on_site": 600 }

### The dispatcher's read of it after that: unchanged
# @name DispatcherRereadsThatVisit
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits/{{VisitOnUnassignedJobId}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The assigned AND booked technician writes their own visit (control)
# @name TechWritesOwnVisit
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits/{{VisitOfTechNorthId}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyTechNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "notes": "Valve replaced, pressure tested." }

### And may not re-point it at a job that is not theirs. The ref is resolved AS THE CALLER first, and a job
### they cannot read is unresolvable — so it is refused before the rule's check on the new row is reached
# @name TechRepointsOwnVisit
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits/{{VisitOfTechNorthId}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyTechNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "work_order_id": "{{Job3402Id}}" }

### The dispatcher's read of tech-north's visit after both writes
# @name DispatcherReadsTechVisit
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/visits/{{VisitOfTechNorthId}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
